[{:db/id "q-161210/selection/20a1164dead41c4073e0347eeb4ea3fb0968a5f113fbe8e693832e31d11a817a" :answer/id #uuid "51740d6a-b8d1-5862-969f-8c927d6c3abd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2xy+{z}^{2}-xz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161210/selection/e457b42de7f1b0a1fb9e8719055c8856d0a1c9a09b61a5c0c228ac05225fa91c" :answer/id #uuid "303d3e86-b7e9-5441-a01a-c4b28a14cd18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xy+2{z}^{2}-xz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161210/selection/d9a3d2bb3d6b27e1ef0ee750b28ce498e11fa7b01fc3047db492f80f44215544" :answer/id #uuid "01a9d1a8-72fb-53fe-af05-ef008e797544" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{z}^{2}-xyz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161210/selection/5ca26b0d488f1b0636881d5bc8393a3b9ecd309528fbc2ccecaa040e86ea5c30" :answer/id #uuid "e1db64a4-9765-5556-9713-080d48773c1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{z}^{2}-xz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161210/selection/9fff254b150ed8d0192701841e893a0312e832f38b1fbdd6c5f427d71f10c05c" :answer/id #uuid "c4f873db-34b8-50bb-8eef-00ec97802a32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2xy-{z}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161210/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e8b50ee-7eca-5889-99fe-1cdcdb9c946d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161210/selection/5ca26b0d488f1b0636881d5bc8393a3b9ecd309528fbc2ccecaa040e86ea5c30" :answer-field/choices ["q-161210/selection/20a1164dead41c4073e0347eeb4ea3fb0968a5f113fbe8e693832e31d11a817a" "q-161210/selection/e457b42de7f1b0a1fb9e8719055c8856d0a1c9a09b61a5c0c228ac05225fa91c" "q-161210/selection/d9a3d2bb3d6b27e1ef0ee750b28ce498e11fa7b01fc3047db492f80f44215544" "q-161210/selection/5ca26b0d488f1b0636881d5bc8393a3b9ecd309528fbc2ccecaa040e86ea5c30" "q-161210/selection/9fff254b150ed8d0192701841e893a0312e832f38b1fbdd6c5f427d71f10c05c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161210" :question/id #uuid "b8d6736e-4bf0-5cd4-a023-43b5c372235a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161210" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with normal vector $\\overset{~}{n},$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨y,\\,x-z,\\,-2x⟩\\,,\\,\\overset{~}{n}(x,y,z)=⟨2x,\\,-z,\\,y⟩\\,,\\,n=\\frac{\\overset{~}{n}}{‖\\overset{~}{n}‖}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}\\frac{\\boxed{}}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nTo compute the above dot product, we must normalize the vector $\\overset{~}{n}.$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{\\overset{~}{n}}{‖\\overset{~}{n}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨2x,\\,-z,\\,y⟩}{\\sqrt{(2x)^{2}+(-z)^{2}+(y)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨2x,\\,-z,\\,y⟩}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨2x,\\,-z,\\,y⟩}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculating the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨y,\\,x-z,\\,-2x⟩\\cdot \\frac{⟨2x,\\,-z,\\,y⟩}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨y,\\,x-z,\\,-2x⟩\\cdot ⟨2x,\\,-z,\\,y⟩}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy-z(x-z)-2xy}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{z}^{2}-xz}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\,\\frac{{z}^{2}-xz}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}S.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161210/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21caaf9c-6b9b-5711-a434-21f0416e6c7e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161210"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-160838"] :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with normal vector $\\overset{~}{n},$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,y,\\,x⟩\\,,\\,\\overset{~}{n}(x,y,z)=⟨2y,\\,-z,\\,2x⟩\\,,\\,n=\\frac{\\overset{~}{n}}{‖\\overset{~}{n}‖}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}\\frac{\\boxed{}}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nTo compute the above dot product, we must normalize the vector $\\overset{~}{n}.$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{\\overset{~}{n}}{‖\\overset{~}{n}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨2y,\\,-z,\\,2x⟩}{\\sqrt{(2y)^{2}+(-z)^{2}+(2x)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨2y,\\,-z,\\,2x⟩}{\\sqrt{4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+4{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨2y,\\,-z,\\,2x⟩}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculating the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨z,\\,y,\\,x⟩\\cdot \\frac{⟨2y,\\,-z,\\,2x⟩}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨z,\\,y,\\,x⟩\\cdot ⟨2y,\\,-z,\\,2x⟩}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2yz-yz+2{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+yz}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}+yz}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}S.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-161200/selection/8b1789fb204077eb757e7014ead8367cbc6bf142197cddf74c5188eeb5cfc4d0" :answer/id #uuid "ca57acbc-6787-50f9-80ff-ecdba16668fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xy+yz+xz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161200/selection/850e7d2adfc49b89c65cc09a4dd9567608eb439a0e74f887253a5f3e618a9aec" :answer/id #uuid "a4a94b08-d9ac-5170-b99f-02cdba39f6f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161200/selection/34efb9b9d591b84ffe725137f86e3bdf1df45537072be69d53ad82f0848ce725" :answer/id #uuid "3b1b160a-37ba-5665-82ec-24ee8680c3ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xy-yz+2xz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161200/selection/8d762ff4f1f6499f0681b0f2fe87869dbe1019435ca6042e9690cb3cebb05b7e" :answer/id #uuid "bf014fd6-fac3-57a8-8adf-1f320e7d21d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xy-2yz+xz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161200/selection/3707c30e7a2ef5d016a24c40f459a4fc8cb0b6e5f02ef1591eeb761538bfbf61" :answer/id #uuid "39872af4-30af-5a84-b1da-d87b13553dc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3xz-yz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161200/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b584cb0-388b-57c3-9ae4-64c65eedac7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161200/selection/34efb9b9d591b84ffe725137f86e3bdf1df45537072be69d53ad82f0848ce725" :answer-field/choices ["q-161200/selection/8b1789fb204077eb757e7014ead8367cbc6bf142197cddf74c5188eeb5cfc4d0" "q-161200/selection/850e7d2adfc49b89c65cc09a4dd9567608eb439a0e74f887253a5f3e618a9aec" "q-161200/selection/34efb9b9d591b84ffe725137f86e3bdf1df45537072be69d53ad82f0848ce725" "q-161200/selection/8d762ff4f1f6499f0681b0f2fe87869dbe1019435ca6042e9690cb3cebb05b7e" "q-161200/selection/3707c30e7a2ef5d016a24c40f459a4fc8cb0b6e5f02ef1591eeb761538bfbf61"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161200" :question/id #uuid "9cf65a4b-2e8e-5496-9a1a-b1343d6ea749" :question/math-academy-id "q-161200" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with unit normal vector $n,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨xy,\\,yz,\\,xz⟩\\,,\\,n(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,2⟩\\,.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}{∬}_{S}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nCalculating the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨xy,\\,yz,\\,xz⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨xy,\\,yz,\\,xz⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}(xy-yz+2xz) \\\\  & =\\frac{xy-yz+2xz}{\\sqrt{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\frac{xy-yz+2xz}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}{∬}_{S}xy-yz+2xz\\,\\text{d}S.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161200/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21caaf9c-6b9b-5711-a434-21f0416e6c7e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161200"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161198/selection/24febe065eeee931baa32f3495a63f62b433e46ee016f2ea269c8ab18be0d1ce" :answer/id #uuid "ab23ec92-0f8f-5ad0-8806-583585df8df2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y+{z}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161198/selection/822c9016350a3bb4bc4c5b5e3c5238c0a1a9b71f91173d499513ddf718965637" :answer/id #uuid "86306ce9-20a4-5730-8c71-b15f99ca3bc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y+{z}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161198/selection/0625498f1f17e6da1aa97e2bb29a474bce2af83bdb56c76f9b2e69b52d5484ff" :answer/id #uuid "0484fd1e-871f-59fa-b962-ccdb195cad3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y-x-2{z}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161198/selection/fe27c42515cfee57902b1c88af87a831b53408f19f412e54f5dc3b9adadb0c58" :answer/id #uuid "15b63f7e-dcca-5164-973e-fbc764e968f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2{z}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161198/selection/98dbb27f5c716c4a471ac0c4a538e6f76db20dece23a706c1bd52aa90b5a10f6" :answer/id #uuid "f49e49b4-b900-53d6-b790-a294ca471046" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161198/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fcc8ddbe-f5cf-597d-adae-a75ffe46c214" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161198/selection/98dbb27f5c716c4a471ac0c4a538e6f76db20dece23a706c1bd52aa90b5a10f6" :answer-field/choices ["q-161198/selection/24febe065eeee931baa32f3495a63f62b433e46ee016f2ea269c8ab18be0d1ce" "q-161198/selection/822c9016350a3bb4bc4c5b5e3c5238c0a1a9b71f91173d499513ddf718965637" "q-161198/selection/0625498f1f17e6da1aa97e2bb29a474bce2af83bdb56c76f9b2e69b52d5484ff" "q-161198/selection/fe27c42515cfee57902b1c88af87a831b53408f19f412e54f5dc3b9adadb0c58" "q-161198/selection/98dbb27f5c716c4a471ac0c4a538e6f76db20dece23a706c1bd52aa90b5a10f6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161198" :question/id #uuid "dd68aee4-128c-55a1-8849-b847e40933c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161198" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with unit normal vector $n,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{z}^{2},\\,x,\\,y-{z}^{2}⟩\\,,\\,n(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,-1,\\,2⟩\\,.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S=\\frac{1}{3}{∬}_{S}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nCalculating the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨{z}^{2},\\,x,\\,y-{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨{z}^{2},\\,x,\\,y-{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2{z}^{2}-x+2(y-{z}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{2y-x}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\frac{2y-x}{3}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{∬}_{S}2y-x\\,\\text{d}S.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161198/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21caaf9c-6b9b-5711-a434-21f0416e6c7e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161198"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161199/selection/d7c3bda8c0ba544445f6d1ad4004f6301c23ac3c15971c262e351d0546b6e662" :answer/id #uuid "9445a197-d84d-5878-8572-b036b048897c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xy-3-{e}^{z}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161199/selection/cf67bffad80b1db54b0472ee187e1534375424d21d45246a9b710df1b3e6d158" :answer/id #uuid "0ee3964b-5ca7-5728-ae0a-437b77f78445" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xy+{e}^{z}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161199/selection/60a13d1d2cd1b7db80778a4fc7c534f5efff60b911db0895edef05a2bf2a23ea" :answer/id #uuid "e6f89fb0-f44e-5ceb-b0fa-cfdbd042c78d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xy+6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161199/selection/97a5126f2d70b35a77272823544e149f8df709da3b73ea87f15b717391c9ce39" :answer/id #uuid "4c759f56-6454-5deb-b9d0-34e63fc3e836" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xy-3