xy,\\,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨3,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}(3(1-{e}^{z})+xy-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{xy-3{e}^{z}}{\\sqrt{11}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\frac{xy-3{e}^{z}}{\\sqrt{11}}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}{∬}_{S}xy-3{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}S.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161199/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21caaf9c-6b9b-5711-a434-21f0416e6c7e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161199"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365878/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "6b9a596f-577b-5d49-b924-e368b82996a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365878/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "73bdeb0f-0f3a-5c4a-85b2-94a6a93e3dea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365878/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "b7e6d076-25d7-5209-ab9d-6fcd2a3f375e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365878/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "52cfb6e5-1e46-55a1-935f-d1d7e172bdb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365878/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "6bf12ae2-6564-54dc-80bd-577d5c44c282" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365878/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6acdd215-c006-518c-a74b-a0fdadc54afe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-365878/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer-field/choices ["q-365878/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-365878/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-365878/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-365878/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-365878/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365878" :question/id #uuid "9dd79803-39bc-570f-ac7b-87b2d6cbc27f" :question/math-academy-id "q-365878" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨y,\\,z,\\,2x⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined in Cartesian coordinates as $z=2$ for $0\\le x\\le 3$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$ Calculate the flux of $F$ through $S$ with respect to the upward-pointing unit normal vector $n.$" :question/worked-solution "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nFor the surface $z=2$ for $0\\le x\\le 3$ and $0\\le y\\le 2,$ the upward-pointing unit normal vector is\n\n$$\nn=⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $z=2$ on $S,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨y,\\,z,\\,2x⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨y,\\,2,\\,2x⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the flux of $F$ across $S$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}2x\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot {[{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-365878/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3da3cc4f-0a1d-5639-b580-95eabc198d2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365878"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365882/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "7a0e74da-8bb7-51e9-9631-3daf463386eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365882/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "a1d7b192-b321-5b96-92ba-a180f407e480" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365882/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "c5d57543-b756-599c-b239-d23fe507bfdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365882/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "749a3585-b8c4-5c32-afa0-4b6dd1493299" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365882/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "d4793f0c-2fa1-5f85-a9cb-3d861ca19f5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365882/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "135e775a-c76d-5370-bd60-fe97d8047202" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-365882/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer-field/choices ["q-365882/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-365882/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" "q-365882/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-365882/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-365882/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365882" :question/id #uuid "ee1444d0-7e94-51bd-9978-54ebc6e79393" :question/math-academy-id "q-365882" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,x,\\,3x+y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined in Cartesian coordinates as $z=-1$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $1\\le y\\le 2.$ Calculate the flux of $F$ through $S$ with respect to the *downward*-pointing unit normal vector $n.$" :question/worked-solution "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is a continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nFor the surface $z=-1$ for  $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $1\\le y\\le 2,$ the downward-pointing unit normal vector is\n\n$$\nn=⟨0,\\,0,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $z=-1$ on $S,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨z,\\,x,\\,3x+y⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =-(3x+y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the flux of $F$ across $S$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}(-(3x+y))\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(3x+y))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(-(3x+y))\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{1}^{2}[(\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+xy){|}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{1}^{2}(6+2y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{[6y+{y}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-365882/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3da3cc4f-0a1d-5639-b580-95eabc198d2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365882"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161192/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e